$ jailops app install postgresql --name db --image freebsd-151@stable
App postgresql installed as jail db (running)
  Version:   18.6
  Addresses: 10.20.0.10
  Ports:     postgres 5432/tcp at 10.20.0.10:5432 The SQL port.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow db from SOURCE
  Data:      /var/db/postgres The cluster (data18).
  Config:    /var/db/postgres/data18/postgresql.conf (restart postgresql) Server settings.
             /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf (restart postgresql) Who may connect.
  Logs:      server /var/log/messages The port logs to syslog.
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback db --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     11 done
Notes:
  Connect from inside the jail with: jailops exec NAME -- su -l postgres -c psql

$ jailops app install nginx --name web --image freebsd-151@stable
App nginx installed as jail web (running)
  Version:   1.30.6,3
  Addresses: 10.20.0.11
  Ports:     http 80/tcp at 10.20.0.11:80 (expose: forwarding is not set up yet) HTTP, the default site.
  Access:    closed: nothing reaches it until jailops app allow web from SOURCE
  Data:      /usr/local/www The sites.
  Config:    /usr/local/etc/nginx/nginx.conf (restart nginx) The server configuration.
  Logs:      access /var/log/nginx/access.log One line per request.
             error /var/log/nginx/error.log
  Snapshot:  app-installed (jailops jail rollback web --all --snapshot app-installed goes back to it)
  Steps:     9 done
Notes:
  Put the site under /usr/local/www.

$ jailops app access
APP   DEFINITION   SOURCE   PORTS   DATABASE   STATE
db    postgresql   -        -       -          closed
web   nginx        -        -       -          closed

$ jailops app allow db from @web --dry-run
Dry run: nothing was changed. Allowing @web to reach db would do:
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 10.20.0.11 to port 5432 (policy app-db)
  pg_hba:    host web web 10.20.0.11/32 scram-sha-256
  Database:  web (role web)
  SQL:       CREATE ROLE "web" LOGIN PASSWORD '<generated, shown once>';
             CREATE DATABASE "web" OWNER "web";
  - firewall policy app-db: allow in tcp from 10.20.0.11 to port 5432
  - in the jail, as postgres: psql with the statements on standard input
  - /var/db/postgres/data18/pg_hba.conf: the managed block gets host web web 10.20.0.11/32 scram-sha-256; then the server reloads it

$ jailops app allow db from @web
Allowed @web to reach db on 5432/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 10.20.0.11 to port 5432 (policy app-db)
  pg_hba:    host web web 10.20.0.11/32 scram-sha-256
  Database:  web (role web)
  SQL:       CREATE ROLE "web" LOGIN PASSWORD '<generated, shown once>';
             CREATE DATABASE "web" OWNER "web";
Connection string (shown once, stored nowhere):
  postgres://web:<password>@10.20.0.10:5432/web?sslmode=disable
Note: the connection string is shown once and stored nowhere; jailops app allow db from @web --rotate makes a new password

$ jailops app allow db from @web
@web may already reach db on 5432/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 10.20.0.11 to port 5432 (policy app-db)
  pg_hba:    host web web 10.20.0.11/32 scram-sha-256
  Database:  web (role web)
Note: role web exists: its password was shown when it was made; --rotate makes a new one
Note: nothing changed: the grant exists as it is

$ jailops app allow db from @web --rotate
Allowed @web to reach db on 5432/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 10.20.0.11 to port 5432 (policy app-db)
  pg_hba:    host web web 10.20.0.11/32 scram-sha-256
  Database:  web (role web)
  SQL:       ALTER ROLE "web" LOGIN PASSWORD '<generated, shown once>';
Connection string (shown once, stored nowhere):
  postgres://web:<password>@10.20.0.10:5432/web?sslmode=disable
Note: the connection string is shown once and stored nowhere; jailops app allow db from @web --rotate makes a new password

$ jailops app allow db from 192.0.2.0/24 --db shop
Allowed 192.0.2.0/24 to reach db on 5432/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 192.0.2.0/24 to port 5432 (policy app-db)
  pg_hba:    host shop shop 192.0.2.0/24 scram-sha-256
  Database:  shop (role shop)
  SQL:       CREATE ROLE "shop" LOGIN PASSWORD '<generated, shown once>';
             CREATE DATABASE "shop" OWNER "shop";
Connection string (shown once, stored nowhere):
  postgres://shop:<password>@10.20.0.10:5432/shop?sslmode=disable
Note: the connection string is shown once and stored nowhere; jailops app allow db from 192.0.2.0/24 --rotate makes a new password

$ jailops app allow web from host
Allowed host to reach web on 80/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 10.20.0.1 to port 80 (policy app-web)
Note: only the firewall changed: the app must itself listen on the jail's address and accept the client (see its configuration files with jailops app info nginx)

$ jailops app allow web from 198.51.100.7 --port 80 --port 443/tcp
Allowed 198.51.100.7 to reach web on 80/tcp, 443/tcp.
  Rule:      allow in tcp from 198.51.100.7 to port 80,443 (policy app-web)
Note: only the firewall changed: the app must itself listen on the jail's address and accept the client (see its configuration files with jailops app info nginx)

$ jailops app access
APP   DEFINITION   SOURCE         PORTS            DATABASE   STATE
db    postgresql   @web           5432/tcp         web        ok
db    postgresql   192.0.2.0/24   5432/tcp         shop       ok
web   nginx        host           80/tcp           -          ok
web   nginx        198.51.100.7   80/tcp,443/tcp   -          ok

